Plot lock: `SELECT ... FROM plot WHERE plot_code=? FOR UPDATE`.

Service registerTransplant(cmd):
```java
@Transactional
public TransplantView register(cmd) {
  // idempotency check first (by requestId, outside lock ok but do inside tx)
  TransplantRow existing = repo.findTransplantByRequestId(cmd.requestId());
  if (existing != null) {
    if (matches(existing, cmd)) return toView(existing);
    throw BizException.conflict("requestId 已使用且参数不一致");
  }
  PlotRow plot = repo.findPlotForUpdate(cmd.plotCode()); // 404 if absent
  if (plot.status == SEALED) throw conflict(409, "样方已封存");
  if (repo.findTransplantByPlantCode(cmd.plantCode()) != null) throw conflict("植株编号已存在");
  if (repo.countActiveTransplants(plot.id) >= plot.capacity) throw unprocessable("样方容量已满");
  insert with status PENDING, transplantedAt = Instant.now(clock)
}
```

Wait — 容量已满 returns 409 or 422? Task: "容量已满、重复植株编号、死亡后再标存活或已封存样方新增移植返回 409/422" — any of 409/422 acceptable. I'll use 409 for capacity full (it's a conflict with current state), 422 for dead→alive and seal-with-pending (semantic state violation). Both in allowed set.

review(plantCode, cmd):
```java
@Transactional
public TransplantView review(plantCode, cmd) {
  ReviewRow existingReview = repo.findReviewByRequestId(cmd.requestId());
  if (existingReview != null) {
    if (existingReview.transplant matches plantCode && existingReview.result == cmd.result) return view;
    throw conflict("requestId 已使用且参数不一致");
  }
  TransplantRow t = repo.findTransplantByPlantCode(plantCode); // 404
  PlotRow plot = repo.findPlotForUpdate(t.plotId); // lock
  if (plot.sealed) throw conflict("样方已封存，禁止复核");
  if (t.status == DEAD && cmd.result == ALIVE) throw unprocessable("死亡植株不得标为存活");
  // DEAD -> DEAD idempotent-ish? If already DEAD and review DEAD again with new requestId — allow? It's a duplicate observation; harmless. Allow DEAD->DEAD, ALIVE->PENDING etc. But DEAD->PENDING? "死亡后释放容量" — if we allow DEAD->PENDING, capacity would need re-check. Simpler: DEAD is final except DEAD->DEAD allowed. Reject DEAD->ALIVE (422 per spec) and DEAD->PENDING (422).
  insert review, update status
}
```

seal(plotCode, cmd):
```java
@Transactional
public SealView seal(plotCode, cmd) {
  PlotRow plot = repo.findPlotForUpdate(plotCode); // 404
  SealRow existing = repo.findSealByPlotId(plot.id);
  if (existing != null) {
    if (existing.requestId == cmd.requestId) return view(existing);
    throw conflict("样方已封存");
  }
  List<TransplantRow> all = repo.findTransplantsByPlotId(plot.id);
  long pending = count PENDING;
  if (pending > 0) throw unprocessable("存在待复核植株，禁止封存");
  counts alive/dead; plant list = all plant codes with status (JSON string built manually or via ObjectMapper)
  insert seal, update plot status=SEALED, sealed_at
}
```

Plant list in snapshot: store JSON array of {plantCode, status}. Use ObjectMapper to serialize. Simple.

getTransplant(plantCode): view with nursery, plotCode, status, transplantedAt, review chain (list of reviews), seal info of plot (sealed counts if sealed).
getPlot(plotCode): status, capacity, activeCount, counts by status, seal snapshot if present.

Controller endpoints:
- POST /api/coral/transplants  (body: requestId, plantCode, nursery, plotCode) → 201 TransplantView
- POST /api/coral/transplants/{plantCode}/reviews (body: requestId, result) → 200 TransplantView
- POST /api/coral/plots/{plotCode}/seal (body: requestId) → 200 SealView
- GET /api/coral/transplants/{plantCode} → TransplantView
- GET /api/coral/plots/{plotCode} → PlotView

Validation: @NotBlank on requestId, plantCode, nursery, plotCode; result @NotNull.

Exception handler: BizException → status + body {error, message}; MethodArgumentNotValidException → 400.

Clock: @Bean Clock clock() { return Clock.systemUTC(); } in a @Configuration. Service uses Instant.now(clock).

DTO views:

```java
public record TransplantView(String plantCode, String nursery, String plotCode, String status,
    Instant transplantedAt, List<ReviewView> reviews, SealSummary seal) {}
public record ReviewView(String requestId, String result, Instant reviewedAt) {}
public record SealSummary(boolean sealed, Instant sealedAt, Integer aliveCount, Integer deadCount, Integer pendingCount) {}
public record SealView(String plotCode, String requestId, Instant sealedAt, int aliveCount, int deadCount, int pendingCount, List<SealPlantItem> plants) {}
public record SealPlantItem(String plantCode, String status) {}
public record PlotView(String plotCode, String status, int capacity, long activeCount, long aliveCount, long deadCount, long pendingCount, SealView seal) {}
```

Seal plant list stored as JSON in DB; parse back with ObjectMapper for views. Store as `List<SealPlantItem>` json.

